      },
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "never",
          "sigil": false,
          "form": "keyword",
          "line": 181,
          "attrs": {},
          "body": {
            "type": "markdown",
            "text": "block a PR on style alone."
          }
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "text": "\nRead the whole diff before commenting on any of it. Then, in this order:\n\n### Correctness\n\nDoes it do what the PR says? Trace one happy path and one failure path by\nhand. If you cannot, say which path you could not trace.\n\n### Tests\n\nIs the new behaviour tested? Is the bug it fixes reproduced by a test that\nfails without the fix? SHOULD: ask for that test if it is missing.\n\n### Everything else\n\nNaming, structure and style come last, and only if the first two are clean.\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "skill",
      "sigil": true,
      "form": "section",
      "line": 183,
      "attrs": {
        "when": "writing a commit or PR description",
        "name": "commit-messages"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "sigil": false,
          "form": "container",
          "line": 189,
          "attrs": {
            "title": "A good commit message"
          },
          "body": {
            "type": "markdown",
            "text": "Reject bare `any` in the linter\n\nUnannotated `any` hides type errors that the rest of the toolchain would\ncatch. The linter now flags it unless a justifying comment follows on the\nsame line, matching the rule in the coding agent's instruction.\n\nRefs T-4821"
          }
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "text": "\nOne line, imperative mood, under seventy characters, saying what the change\ndoes — not what you did. Then a blank line, then why, in as many lines as it\ntakes. Reference the ticket at the end.\n\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "workflow",
      "sigil": true,
      "form": "section",
      "line": 199,
      "attrs": {
        "name": "ci-triage",
        "description": "Wakes when a CI run on one of your branches fails, reads the log, and either\nfixes it or asks the reviewer."
      },
      "body": {
        "type": "yaml",
        "text": "steps:\n  wake: { kind: subscribe, server: ci, uri: \"ci://runs/failed?branch=mine\" }\n  read: { kind: mcp.tool, depends_on: [wake], server: ci, tool: read_log, args: { run: \"{{steps.wake.output.run_id}}\" } }\n  decide:\n    kind: agent\n    depends_on: [read]\n    instruction: |\n      Fix the failure if it is in your change. Otherwise reply with the single\n      line NEEDS-HUMAN, then a summary for the reviewer.\n      {{steps.read.output}}\n  ask:\n    kind: human\n    depends_on: [decide]\n    when: \"steps.decide.output.startsWith('NEEDS-HUMAN')\"\n    question: \"{{steps.decide.output}}\"\n    to: \"@human/reviewer\"\n    timeout: 4h\n  done: { kind: finish, depends_on: [decide, ask] }"
      }
    },
